    "result_text": "The build is green. Here's a summary of what I did.\n\n## Change: unify `customerCode` + `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId`\n\n**Format `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`** \u2014 e.g. `NSW2716E6609E1`:\n- `REGION` \u2014 postcode-derived region code (NSW/VIC/QLD/UNKNOWN)\n- `FY` \u2014 2-digit registration-date fiscal year\n- `HASH8` \u2014 the same first-8 upper-hex of `SHA-256(normalizedTelephone + lastName)` used by the region-and-hash identity\n- `CHK` \u2014 one Luhn check digit over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`\n\n**Files touched:**\n- `openapi.yml` \u2014 replaced the `customerCode` + `checkDigit` schema with a single `memberId`; removed `membershipNumber` (`OwnerDto` regenerates from this).\n- `Owner.java` \u2014 renamed the `customerCode` field/column/accessors to `memberId`/`member_id`.\n- `OwnerMemberIdPolicy.java` (new, replaces `OwnerCustomerCodePolicy`) \u2014 one cohesive class that assigns the `memberId`, reusing the existing region lookup and HASH8, plus small `fiscalYear`/`luhn` helpers. Collision handling now dedups on `memberId`.\n- Deleted `OwnerCheckDigitPolicy` and `OwnerMembershipPolicy` (their outputs are now the `CHK`/removed fields).\n- `OwnerMapper.java` \u2014 dropped the `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` mappings; `memberId` auto-maps from `Owner.memberId`.\n- `OwnerLocalityPolicy.java` \u2014 derives the region from `memberId`'s leading letters (before the FY digits) instead of the old dashed customer code, so `ownerSegment`/`timezone` keep working off the member id.\n- `OwnerAuditPolicy.java` \u2014 audit lines now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1.java` \u2014 calls `OwnerMemberIdPolicy.assignMemberId`.\n- `db/hsqldb/schema.sql` \u2014 `customer_code` column renamed to `member_id` (widened to 30).\n\n**Structural impact kept low:** each edited method stays CC-1\u20133, the new construction logic lives in a fresh small class (low WMC_other) rather than being bolted onto the controller/mapper/Owner, and the consumer edits (locality, audit) are localized single-method changes.\n\nTest result: `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 **BUILD SUCCESS**. The new `coreReturnsUnifiedMemberId` test passes (memberId starts with `NSW`, contains the HASH8, and the old fields are absent).",
